        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): explain replace-mode filtering in model picker",
        "body": "Closes #104545\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen `models.mode: \"replace\"` filters the model catalog, the Control UI showed the resulting models without explaining why other bundled or discovered models might be absent.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nConfigured model-list responses now carry additive `catalogMode: \"replace\"` metadata. The chat model picker and Quick Settings use that metadata to explain that model settings are filtering the catalog, without claiming that every visible row was explicitly configured. Full-catalog (`view: \"all\"`) responses do not carry the hint metadata.\n\nThe picker action opens the Models section directly at `/settings/ai-agents?section=models#config-section-models`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can tell that local model settings are filtering the catalog and can navigate directly to the relevant settings instead of treating an absent model as an upstream support problem.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `main` at `d1684f48a31`; exact pushed head: `b324dd386f6`.\n- Both final rebases were conflict-free, and `git range-diff` showed all three commits patch-equivalent to the reviewed series.\n- Focused Gateway regressions: 2 files, 48 tests passed.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/models.test.ts`\n- Focused Control UI regressions: 5 files, 262 tests passed.\n  - `pnpm --dir ui exec vitest run --config vitest.config.ts src/pages/chat/chat-state.test.ts src/pages/chat/chat-view.test.ts src/pages/chat/models.test.ts src/pages/config/quick.test.ts src/pages/model-providers/data.test.ts`\n- Targeted Chromium replace-mode regression: 1 passed, 6 skipped.\n  - `pnpm exec vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.ui-e2e.config.ts --configLoader runner ui/src/e2e/chat-composer-redesign.e2e.test.ts -t 'explains model filtering in replace mode'`\n- `pnpm protocol:check` passed with generated outputs stable.\n- TypeScript LOC ratchet passed for all 13 changed production files.\n- Focused `oxfmt` passed for all 21 changed TypeScript/CSS files; type-aware `oxlint` passed for all 20 changed TypeScript files.\n- `pnpm deadcode:unused-files` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- The final locale diff changes only `ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts`; generated non-English locale files remain on the repository workflow.\n- A fresh local `codex review --base origin/main` found no concrete regression in the gateway/UI flow or route target; subsequent rebases were patch-equivalent by `git range-diff`.\n- Desktop 1280x900 and mobile 393x852 proof remains in the earlier immutable proof comment. Both show the replace-mode hint and Manage models action with clean wrapping and no overlap.\n\nCurrent-base note: repository-wide `pnpm tsgo:ui` and `pnpm deadcode:exports` are presently blocked by unrelated `main` regressions outside this PR. `src/config/sessions/store.ts` references three missing identifiers, while two newly extracted gateway helpers are exported only for tests. This PR does not modify those files; the same model-picker patch passed both UI typecheck lanes on the immediately preceding base.\n\nBefore: the UI silently presented the filtered catalog.\n\nAfter: the picker and Quick Settings state, \"Replace mode filters models according to your model settings,\" and link directly to the Models settings section.\n\nAI-assisted: Codex was used to implement, test, and review this change. No agent transcript is attached.\n",
        "branch": "agent/model-picker-replace-mode-hint",
